``` Introduction

`File_System` isn't part of the default preload -- it needs an explicit `@load`. Its two static methods write a String to a file and read one back.
```
@load 'ore/file_system.ore'

message := 'If anyone finds this, we crashed on an island.'
@puts "writing: `message`"   # writing: If anyone finds this, we crashed on an island.
File_System.write_string_to_file('./temp/message_in_a_bottle.txt', message)

content := File_System.read('./temp/message_in_a_bottle.txt')
@puts "read back: `content`"   # read back: If anyone finds this, we crashed on an island.

@assert message == content
